        "imageUrl": "https://images.autotrader.com/scaler/400/400/cars/ford-mustang-2020-prem-conv.jpg",
        "source": "autotrader",
        "whyGood": "A 2020 Mustang Premium convertible at $8,995 is a stunning value regardless of mileage — this is a modern car with Apple CarPlay, heated seats, and Ford's folding power top. Even at 132k the S550 chassis is durable. Premium spec at this price is rare. Dealer (Fred Beans) adds some confidence.",
        "whatToVerify": "MT-82 (if manual) shifter feel is mediocre but improve with Steeda shifter bushings — confirm trans. 2.3T EcoBoost: check for spark plug blowout history (solved post-2018), coolant leaks. 5.0 GT would be preferable at this price. Ask dealer what engine/trim exactly. Top: full cycle, rear window, drain channels. 8.8 rear axle clunk at takeoff.",
        "bottomLine": "A 2020 Mustang convertible under $9k is unusual — pull the Carfax, PPI the engine bay, and if clean it's a daily-drivable fun car at modern amenity levels."
      },
      {
        "rank": 6,
        "year": 2010,
        "make": "Audi",
        "model": "S5",
        "trim": "3.0T quattro Premium Plus Cabriolet AWD",
        "price": 10489,
        "mileage": 92034,
        "location": "Marlton, NJ",
        "distanceMi": 27,
        "url": "https://www.cargurus.com/details/459964081",
        "dealer": null,
        "dealRating": "Good Deal",
        "transmission": null,
        "imageUrl": "https://static.cargurus.com/images/forsale/2024/10/01/01/50/2010_audi_s5-pic-459964081.jpeg",
        "source": "cargurus",
        "whyGood": "The S5 Cabriolet with the 3.0T supercharged V6 is a genuinely quick and special car — 333hp AWD convertible with Audi's best top and interior. 92k miles is fine for this drivetrain. Good Deal badge from CarGurus. Supercharged V6 is smoother and more reliable than the S4's V8.",
        "whatToVerify": "Supercharger snout leak (look for oil on the front of the blower). Timing chain on 3.0T — any stretch codes? Carbon buildup (DI only helps with walnut blast). Haldex fluid change. Top cycle, rear window, drain channels. MMI unit reliability. S-tronic (if DSG) mechatronic unit — any reported issues?",
        "bottomLine": "A supercharged V6 AWD convertible at $10k is the kind of absurd value depreciation creates — worth every dollar if the PPI checks out."
      },
      {
        "rank": 7,
        "year": 2013,
        "make": "INFINITI",
        "model": "G37",
        "trim": "Convertible",
        "price": 13289,
        "mileage": 91309,
        "location": "Cherry Hill, NJ",
        "distanceMi": 23,
        "url": "https://www.cargurus.com/details/460280083",
        "dealer": null,
        "dealRating": "Fair Deal",
        "transmission": null,
        "imageUrl": "https://static.cargurus.com/images/forsale/2024/10/01/01/50/2013_infiniti_g37-pic-460280083.jpeg",
        "source": "cargurus",
        "whyGood": "The G37 convertible is one of the best-built 4-seat drop-tops ever made — VQ37VHR NA V6 is legendary for reliability and sound, the folding hardtop is tight and rattle-free, and INFINITI's interior quality is excellent. 91k on a 2013 means a long life ahead. The G37 is arguably the most bulletproof choice in this list.",
        "whatToVerify": "VQ37 notorious for valve cover gasket oil leaks (easy fix, common). Check for any transmission jerks or flares (7AT in the G37 is very reliable — but verify). Top: retractable hardtop mechanism — listen for any motor hesitation or grinding in mid-cycle. Trunk is tiny with top down. Rear window heating element.",
        "bottomLine": "The G37 convertible is the safest, most reliable 4-seat drop-top in this budget — if the PPI shows clean mechanicals and the top cycles properly, buy without hesitation."
      },
      {
