        "whyGood": "Same model family as rank 8 but one year older and 33k more miles at $200 less — both are solid. AWD on the 2015 is an advantage in shoulder season. 105k on the EA888 is fine if maintained. Fair Deal on CarGurus at Cherry Hill.",
        "whatToVerify": "Same PCV/carbon checks as 2016. Higher mileage means timing chain tensioner more important to verify. S-tronic mechartronic at 105k — any fault codes? Top drainage at this mileage more critical (clogs compound). Check for any rust on rear subframe mounting points.",
